# Technical Debt

Draft from Phase 1 (working-with-legacy-code) for `play/src/front/Phaser/Game/GameScene.ts`, 2026-11-12. Baseline: the checkout's `GameScene.ts`, sha256 `652254f9…97940e8`, which is the same as `HEAD`. The evidence for each row is in `docs/audits/tech-debt/phase1-gamescene/README.md`.

## Debt Ledger

| Item | Location | Type | Risk | Effort | Priority | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| GS-01: a first walk heading DOWN is not shared until the player turns or stops. `lastSentTick` stays undefined until the first send, so `currentTick - lastSentTick` is `NaN` and the throttle never passes. The placeholder `lastMoveEventSent` faces DOWN, so the turn rule does not fire either. Other users see the avatar stand still and then jump. Map scripts get no `hasPlayerMoved` event. | `GameScene.ts:326` (`lastSentTick!: number`), `:327-334` (placeholder), `:4394` (throttle) | bug | medium. Seen by everyone near a user who first walks down after entering. The server and scripts get no position until a turn or a stop. | XS (one field initializer) | P1 | pinned (`GameSceneMovement.test.ts`, "GS-01"); fix ready: `fix-GS-01.patch` (test flips) |
| GS-02: `removeAllRemotePlayers()` removes the players but keeps their interpolations. The next `update()` throws `Cannot find player with ID "<id>"`. | `GameScene.ts:3931-3941`, `:1502-1505` | bug (latent) | high impact, low likelihood. A throw in `update()` stops the game loop (see GS-03). It can only happen when `create()` runs on a scene instance that has interpolations in progress. No `scene.restart` caller was found in `play/src/front`. | XS (one line) | P2 | pinned ("GS-02"); fix ready: `fix-GS-02.patch` (test flips) |
| GS-03: if anything inside `GameScene.update()` throws, the Phaser loop stops for good. `RequestAnimationFrame.step` runs the callback before it schedules the next frame (`node_modules/phaser/src/dom/RequestAnimationFrame.js:97-101`). The canvas freezes while the Svelte UI keeps working. `update()` throws explicitly at `:1504`, and `doAddPlayer` rethrows texture errors at `:4491-4497`. | `GameScene.ts:1379-1540`, `Game.ts:52` | reliability / design | high. This is a freeze mechanism that matches "the canvas freezes, the menus still work" (the H02 discriminator). It is not tied to the eight-user incident: no browser console from the incident exists. | S (guard and report in `Game.step`, or no throws in the frame path) | P1 (Phase 7) | open. Next discriminator: an uncaught error in the browser console at the moment of a freeze. |
| GS-04: every local move event (one per frame while walking) builds an array of every remote player, actionable item and activatable entity. It passes the array to `updateActivatableObjectsDistances`. The cost grows with the size of the room, not with the number of neighbours. | `GameScene.ts:4294-4299` | performance / scaling (1,000 users) | medium. O(N) allocation and distance work per frame while walking. | M (ask the spatial index for nearby players) | P2 | pinned ("measures the distance to every remote player…"); fix not started |
| GS-05: `update()` checks every conversation bubble for each remote player that moved that frame (`addConversationBubblesAffectedByPlayerMove`). The cost is O(moving players × groups) per frame. | `GameScene.ts:1499-1534`, `:1542-1557` | performance / scaling | medium at 1,000 users. Related to H01/A01 (bubble redraw). | M | P2 | not pinned (gap: bubble path) |
| GS-06: when a remote player has no newer message, extrapolation draws it up to `MAX_EXTRAPOLATION_TIME` (100 ms) of travel past the last position it reported. The last frame marks it `moving: false` at that extrapolated spot (pinned: x = 401 for a reported 300). | `PlayersPositionInterpolator.ts:20-29`, `PlayerMovement.ts` via `GameScene.ts:4615-4623` | behavior quirk (designed extrapolation) | low, but relevant to H15: with dropped moves, avatars rest off position until the next message | S | P3 | pinned; decide whether to keep it before any change |
| GS-07: `onPlayerMovementEnded` callbacks run on every move event, though the comment says "if movement just ended". No caller registers one. | `GameScene.ts:4301-4304`, `:4857-4859` | dead API / misleading comment | low | XS | P3 | open |
| GS-08: `GameScene` only imports into Vitest with more than about 1.5 GB of heap. The import takes about 36 s. With the default heap in a 3 GB container, the run hit an OOM (exit 134). The class is wired to most of the front end. | `GameScene.ts:1-250` (imports) | test debt / coupling | medium. The GameScene tests are slow, and on small runners they need `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=2700` or more. | L (Phase 2-5 extraction) | P2 | open; recorded as a CI gate condition |

